UID:53R4RFWabV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 75 mins (1h15m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival 
 presents short films by Gdynia Film School students: Blueberries (Marta Ko
 walska)\, The Color of Cherries (Filip Błaszczyk)\, Fear (Robert Zawadzki
 ) and Penguin Habits (Jakub Poterała). BlueberriesSara has a bright futur
 e ahead with her wonderful boyfriend. On this beautiful day\, they are set
  to celebrate their engagement at his family home."The Color of Cherries"A
 fter the death of their mother\, two sisters meet in their old family home
  in the countryside. One’s return after years of absence becomes an oppo
 rtunity to confront a difficult past marked by violence and family secrets
 .FearThe narrative explores the themes of humanity and moral conflict amid
 st a humanitarian crisis at the Polish-Belarusian border.Penguin Habits"Mo
 m saves penguins" – that’s how Emilia’s job would be described by he
 r son\, Antek. The day has come for Emilia to depart for a research statio
 n in Antarctica\, and the boy must stay at home under his grandfather’s 
 care.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-polish-film-festi
 val-2026/gsf-shorts\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Altar Boys
DTSTART:20261024T010000Z
DTEND:20261024T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T010000Z
UID:DWx1sK9X4p
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival
  presents the film The Altar Boys. The story follows a group of altar bo
 ys who\, disillusioned by the Church's indifference\, decide to take matt
 ers into their own hands. They plant a bug in the confessional to learn th
 eir neighbors' secrets and dispense justice by their own rules. Their miss
 ion quickly spirals out of control. The screening will be followed by a Q
 &A with director Piotr Domalewski and actress Kamila Urzędowska.\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-polish-film-festival-2026/the-a
 ltar-boys\n\nEstimated start: 18:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Erupcja
DTSTART:20261024T033000Z
DTEND:20261024T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T033000Z
UID:fdtTpxwyFK
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 71 mins (1h11m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival 
 presents the film Erupcja. A volcanic eruption strands Bethany and her 
 soon-to-be fiancé\, Rob\, in Warsaw\, Poland. Taking the explosive event 
 as a sign\, she soon reunites with her childhood friend\, Nel\, and embark
 s on a European adventure that forces her to confront the pains and pleasu
 res of growing up.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-poli
 sh-film-festival-2026/erupcja\n\nEstimated start: 20:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gorky Resort
DTSTART:20261025T210000Z
DTEND:20261025T231000Z
DTSTAMP:20261025T210000Z
UID:NRaGJITOCs
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival
  presents the film Gorky Resort. In 1939\, as war descends on Europe\, th
 ousands of Polish citizens are taken captive by the Soviet Union and subje
 cted to relentless ideological indoctrination. An ambitious Soviet agent s
 ets out to break the spirit of a young\, world-renowned pianist and leader
  among the prisoners\, believing that his surrender could force others to 
 follow.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-polish-film-fes
 tival-2026/gorky-resort\n\nEstimated start: 14:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Larp
DTSTART:20261025T230000Z
DTEND:20261026T005500Z
DTSTAMP:20261025T230000Z
UID:xR9x7c8t3r
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival
  presents the film Larp. The story follows Sergiusz\, a teenager who loves
  fantasy and LARPing\, and struggles with bullying at school and his feeli
 ngs for Helena. When he discovers her secret\, he gets a chance for an ext
 raordinary adventure.The screening will be followed by a Q&A with actress 
 Martyna Byczkowska.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-pol
 ish-film-festival-2026/larp\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild\, Wild East
DTSTART:20261026T011500Z
DTEND:20261026T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20261026T011500Z
UID:sbTSJJyWEw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festiva
 l presents the film Wild\, Wild East. Wolff\, a mysterious official fr
 om Berlin\, arrives in a sleepy small town in eastern Poland. He carefully
  guards the reasons for his visit\, but his mere presence quickly distur
 bs the peace in Małe Zalesie.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theater
 s/seattle-polish-film-festival-2026/wild-wild-east\n\nEstimated start: 18:
 30
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You Can See Everything
DTSTART:20261029T224500Z
DTEND:20261030T015500Z
DTSTAMP:20261029T224500Z
UID:rLVk78r0e8
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 174 mins (2h54m)\n\nThirty-four days before she’s 
 sent to prison\, notorious Silicon Valley founder Elizabeth Holmes invites
  a skeptical film crew to document her every move. What begins as an intim
 ate portrait of an enigmatic felon becomes a mind-bending three-year journ
 ey into the abyss. From boundary-pushing directors Nathan Fielder and Lanc
 e Oppenheim comes You Can See Everything.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/i
 n-theaters/you-can-see-everything\n\nEstimated start: 16:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wicker
DTSTART:20261030T024500Z
DTEND:20261030T044500Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T024500Z
UID:8d0LL4Jw2l
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nAn ostracized fisherwoman commis
 sions the local basketmaker to weave her a husband\, but when her wicker c
 reation proves unexpectedly extraordinary\, his presence ignites jealousy 
 and upheaval that threatens their quiet village. Q&A with Producer Brent 
 Stiefel following the Friday\, 10/23 7:30pm screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/cinema/in-theaters/wicker\n\nEstimated start: 20:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
